  "notes": "Drawn from the A321neo N434AN (left, Dec 2025) and checked from below on N455AN (Mar 2025). The fin's stripes are horizontal: four red, white between, the blue field forward of a line from just above the root to mid-chord at the tip. The registration and fleet number aft are not drawn. Widebodies carry the same design, the title larger. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the title's length (0.202 of the fuselage), baseline and cap height, and the Flight Symbol, measured on N434AN (A321neo) from both sides; both are about 9 m and 1.3 m on the aircraft, so on a shorter type (737-800, A320) they cover a larger share (about 0.23 of a 737-800, title from x 0.20). The fin's stripes are measured on the A320-family fin; on the 737-800 the same evenly spaced stripes sit 0.03-0.1 higher in fin space and a fifth red stripe crosses the fin root (the A321's upper fuselage stripe), which one type-independent scheme can't show on both.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The 2013 livery replaced the polished-metal 'AA' scheme (1968–2013); the last bare-metal aircraft were repainted by 2015, so only the heritage and Astrojet retros recall it."
